\description{
Read a MetaMorpheus AllQuantifiedProteinGroups.tsv as one row per protein group per sample group, with each sample group's spectral count and intensity as columns.

The many-files form of \code{\link{readers_read_protein_groups}}: the whole list goes to ONE bridge
process, which reads \code{threads} files at once and returns one table, rows grouped by file in
input order whatever \code{threads} is. Never loop the one-file function over files instead.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_read_batch}. \code{records} is the long table: \code{source_index}, the 1-based
  position of the row's file in \code{paths}, and \code{source_path}, then the same columns as
  \code{\link{readers_read_protein_groups}} - \code{q_value} a fraction, \code{spectral_count} in PSMs, \code{intensity}
  in the instrument's intensity units. \code{files} is a data.frame with one row per input: its
  \code{path}, \code{file_type}, \code{reader}, \code{record_count} in groups, \code{sample_labels}, \code{caveats},
  \code{absent_fields}, \code{failed_fields}, \code{excluded_fields} and, for an input that could not be read,
  \code{error_kind}, \code{error_type} and \code{error_message}. \code{file_count}, \code{read_count} and \code{failed_count}
  count files; \code{record_count} counts groups over the files read and \code{returned_count} the groups
  returned; \code{row_count} counts rows.

}
